   "curator_note": "Figure 9.6 on the same page is the (unlabelled-conditions) EI mass spectrum of 2-methylcyclohexanol, M+. m/z 114; the page does not restate the electron energy, and 70 eV is the book's standard EI condition. Only the m/z 57 base peak can be read quantitatively off Figure 9.6; the other fragment m/z values are printed under the schemes without abundances, so no relative_intensity is recorded for them."
